<!--
  The launcher icon's life: one ciliate, mid-meal, with a drifting alga still to come.

  Not stock art and not an abstraction — the picture states a mechanic the sim actually has.
  A Cilio's food vacuole glows in its last meal's colour (Sprites.MEAL), so the cyan light inside
  the purple body is a swallowed Drifta, and the cyan mote above it is the next one. The green
  mote below is a Solara mote off the mat. Three of the world's five species and the whole grazing
  chain, in the three colours the core's bucket table gives them:
      Cilio  #D7A6E8    Drifta #5BC8E8    Solara #46D68C
  Species colours belong to the world (rule 7), which is why the icon carries no amber at all.

  Painted the way Sprites bakes a body in the dark field: a bloom, an interior that is the species
  colour in shadow, a bright membrane, and light instead of outlines inside it.

  Geometry: adaptive-icon foreground, 108x108, everything inside the 66dp safe circle — held
  there by IconTest, which measures the furthest opaque pixel. The body is a tilted ellipse
  (group rotation -20°); its 34 bristles were generated evenly around it, each curved along
  the beat and unevenly long so the fringe reads as hair and not as a gear rim, and pasted here as literal segments
  so this file needs no build step.
-->
